From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cix: phy-cix-usb3: check ref_clk error in cix_u3phy_probe()

cix_u3phy_probe() mistakenly checked IS_ERR(u3phy->apb_clk) a second time
after fetching u3phy->ref_clk with devm_clk_get(). If ref_clk returns an
error such as -EPROBE_DEFER, probe succeeds with an ERR_PTR stored in
u3phy->ref_clk instead of deferring or failing, causing subsequent
sky1_u3phy_init() calls to fail permanently.

Check IS_ERR(u3phy->ref_clk) and propagate its error with dev_err_probe().

Signed-off-by: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usb3.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usb3.c b/drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usb3.c
index 87f43fe..152bbac 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usb3.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usb3.c
@@ -378,10 +378,9 @@ static int cix_u3phy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	u3phy->ref_clk = devm_clk_get(dev, "ref_clk");
-	if (IS_ERR(u3phy->apb_clk)) {
-		dev_err(dev, "phy apb clock not found\n");
-		return PTR_ERR(u3phy->apb_clk);
-	}
+	if (IS_ERR(u3phy->ref_clk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(u3phy->ref_clk),
+				     "phy ref clock not found\n");
 
 	u3phy->base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(u3phy->base))
-- 
2.43.0

